 "content": "# Tile classification\n\nWhen full-width and full-height separator lines partition a grid into equal tiles and the output dimensions match the tile layout, map each tile to one output cell. Use demonstrations to identify which in-tile feature or count determines the output; do not assume every unusual cell or single marker is positive. For the observed task pattern with color-8 separators, 2×3 tiles containing mostly color 3 and occasional color 2, emit 1 for a tile with at least two 2s and 3 otherwise. Treat that specific threshold and color mapping as task-specific evidence, not a general rule for other tile grids.\n"
}

