 "content": "# Symmetry repair\n\nWhen a grid is otherwise horizontally mirror-symmetric but a localized region breaks the symmetry, test row-wise reflection across the vertical centerline as a reconstruction rule. If the demonstration output confirms it, copy each cell's mirrored counterpart only into the corrupted/asymmetric positions and preserve all already matching pairs and unrelated cells. Verify the completed grid is horizontally symmetric and reproduces the demonstrated output; do not impose symmetry based on appearance alone.\n"
}

